{
  "schema": "orca.head_envelope.v1",
  "id": "sovol-sv06",
  "name": "Sovol SV06 / SV06 Plus direct-drive head (planetary extruder, LJ12A3-4 inductive probe, front 4010 blower duct)",
  "provenance": "Sovol SV06 / SV06 Plus direct-drive head (planetary extruder, LJ12A3-4 inductive probe, front 4010 blower duct) Confidence: high. Sources: https://github.com/Sovol3d/SV06-Fully-Open-Source  (Assemblies step/JXHSV06-08000 Extruder Component.step, JXHSV06-03000 X axis assembly.step); https://github.com/Sovol3d/SV06-PLUS  (SV06 PLUS 3D/STEP/JXHSV06P-08000 Extrusion Assembly/JXHSV06P-08000 Extrusion Assembly.step); https://github.com/Sovol3d/Sv06-Source-Code/blob/main/Marlin/Configuration.h  (NOZZLE_TO_PROBE_OFFSET {25,-25,0}, used to confirm handedness). Measured from Sovol's official STEP assemblies (OpenCascade tessellation, 0.05 mm deflection), nozzle tip = lowest point of the 0.4 nozzle. STEP frame -> printer frame: X=-x, Y=-z, Z=-y (nozzle points +y in the STEP; carriage/LM8UU at -z = back; handedness confirmed by the probe landing at (+27,-20) vs the Marlin offset (+25,-25)). levels = union of SV06 and SV06 Plus; each level footprint = bbox of all head material at heights [z, next z) (also conservative if a consumer extends each box upward). levels carry no extra margin. parts = per-component boxes (no margin), each tagged with variant (\"SV06\" / \"SV06 Plus\"); low parts are split at z0+1/+3/+8 mm and U-shaped ducts and rings are decomposed into rectangles on a 1 mm grid, so the gap around the nozzle stays empty. One box covers everything above 40 mm. Fasteners inside larger parts were absorbed into them. A coverage check put every CAD section point below 40 mm inside some box (8 of 1.8M points miss by under the 1 mm grid). Gantry: smooth X rods (SV06: 2x 8 mm, 37 mm apart vertically; Plus: 10 mm rods). Lower rod bottom: SV06 24.84, Plus 34.34; reported value is the lower (SV06). y range is the union of both. The X-end blocks (motor mount / tensioner) at the bed extremes reach ~10 mm lower than the lower rod (~z 14.8 for SV06) but sit outside the X travel. exposed_nozzle_length is to the bottom of the SV06 sock nipple (1.76). The heater block underside is at 7.96 (SV06) / 8.29 (Plus). Footnote: the probe height is user-adjustable; CAD places it ~2.1 mm above the tip. Nozzle: land radius 0.47 mm, 50.2-degree cone to Z=1.76, then the nozzle parts as recorded. Gantry: X beam underside 24.84 mm above the tip, Y 27.5..38.5, every X. Converted by scripts/nonplanar_heads/open_heads.py from research/head-envelopes/sovol-sv06.json (2026-10-13). Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Not calibrated.",
  "calibrated": false,
